# StockZen — MVVM

Keep UI, business logic, and data access in separate layers.

```
lib/
├── core/                 # constants, theme, utils, widgets — no feature logic
├── data/
│   ├── services/         # API, DB, storage
│   └── repositories/     # orchestrate services
└── features/<name>/
    ├── models/
    ├── viewmodels/       # UI state + use cases
    ├── views/            # screens only
    └── widgets/          # optional
```

- **View**: screens/widgets only. No API, DB, business rules, or direct service/repository calls.
- **ViewModel**: UI state and use-case logic; talks to repositories; exposes state to the View.
- **Model**: domain/data models under feature `models/` or `data/`.
- **Repository**: abstracts data sources and orchestrates services.
- **Service**: I/O only (API, local DB, storage).
- **Core**: shared constants, theme, utils, and reusable widgets.

New screens go in `features/<name>/views/`. Do not flatten feature code into `lib/`.
